{"type":"story-file","description":"Story file exists and matches the provided specification","details":"docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md content exactly matches the story text in the prompt, including acceptance criteria and requirements REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS, REQ-FLAT-CONFIG, REQ-CUSTOMIZABLE-PATHS, REQ-RULE-OPTIONS, REQ-PROJECT-INTEGRATION, REQ-CONFIG-VALIDATION."}, {"type":"implementation","description":"Flat-config presets and rule severity mapping (REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS, REQ-FLAT-CONFIG)","details":"src/index.ts defines rule severities and flat-config presets:

```ts
const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES: Readonly<Record> = {
 "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
 "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
 "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
 "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
 "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
 "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
 "traceability/require-test-traceability": "error",
} as const;

/**
 * @story docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md
 * @req REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS - Provide flat-config presets that self-register the plugin and core rules
 */
function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
 return {
 rules: {
 ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES,
 },
 };
}

const configs = {
 recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
 strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
};

plugin.configs = configs;
```

`configs.recommended` and `configs.strict` are ESLint v9-style flat-config **arrays of config objects** exposing rule severities only, intended to be spread into consumer flat configs after a `{ plugins: { traceability } }` entry, exactly matching REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS and REQ-FLAT-CONFIG."}, {"type":"implementation","description":"Dynamic rule registration and rule list traceability (supporting config integration)","details":"src/index.ts enumerates and dynamically loads all rules, with traceability back to this story:

```ts
/**
 * @story docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md
 * @req REQ-RULE-LIST - Enumerate supported rule file names for plugin discovery
 */
const RULE_NAMES = [
 "require-story-annotation",
 "require-req-annotation",
 "require-branch-annotation",
 "valid-annotation-format",
 "valid-story-reference",
 "valid-req-reference",
 "prefer-implements-annotation",
 "require-test-traceability",
] as const;

RULE_NAMES.forEach(
 /**
 * @story docs/stories/002.0-DEV-ESLINT-CONFIG.story.md
 * @req REQ-DYNAMIC-LOADING - Support dynamic rule loading by name at runtime
 */
 (name) => {
 try {
 const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
 rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
 } catch (error: any) {
 // error reporting handled by Story 007.0 (fallback rule)
 }
 },
);
```

This supports clean integration of all rules into the flat configs exported via `plugin.configs`."}, {"type":"tests","description":"Flat config presets integration tests (REQ-CONFIG-PRESETS, REQ-FLAT-CONFIG, REQ-PROJECT-INTEGRATION)","details":"File exists: tests/config/flat-config-presets-integration.test.ts

